+## Current bounded lesson review (2026-10-24)
+
+**Finding: one generated three-demo lesson does not teach the required mirror
+fallback.** Source SHA-256:
+`5517f198d0641385a022bfb233f5ce082121e2baf8001fea08f97a738691a886`;
+selected canonical rule hash `4829c9bc9298`. Native generation with seed `11`,
+automatic demo count, one query, and no overrides accepts sample indices
+`0,1,2,3`. Its corner / h-band / corner demonstrations all fit the executable
+rival “copy each marker cell's left-right mirror, replacing still-blue mirror
+values with zero.” The v-band query needs a clean vertical/180-degree mirror;
+the rival differs from the canonical 5x5 answer in ten cells. All four inputs
+pass `self_check`.
+
+The exact selected canonical program and the rival were replayed on all four
+pairs through protected Racket (eight replay evaluations, in addition to four
+native generation labels). The source-bound episode, exact programs, runtime
+identity, outputs, and differing coordinates are retained in
+`checks/f283b8535697/lr-shortcut/review.json`; the command receipt is
+`checks/f283b8535697/lr-shortcut-command.json`. Reproducer:
+`generators/f283b8535697/workspace/bounded_lr_shortcut.py`.
+
+Suggested follow-up: select a v-band demonstration when a query requires
+fallback beyond the left-right mirror, and check this finite rival while
+assembling lessons. The comment that the rival is refuted “by construction”
+holds across suitable placement families, but does not guarantee it within
+every randomly assembled three-demo lesson. No generator, canonical rule,
+approval, or shared runtime was changed. This bounded result establishes a
+teaching gap for this episode and rival only; it is not a canonical-label error,
+population-rate estimate, or universal ambiguity claim. Repair remains proposed.
